cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use puffball in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "puffball: an Amazon Braket job, ledger and provenance CLI"
abstract: >-
  puffball (command puff) is the spore.host tool for Amazon Braket. It
  discovers devices in every Braket region, prices work before it runs,
  submits OpenQASM 3 and AHS programs, tracks tasks across regions, keeps an
  account-side spend estimate, wraps QPU spending limits, and writes a
  provenance record for every hardware result. Nothing billable happens
  without --real. Part of the spore.host suite.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Scott
    family-names: Friedman
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1480-765X"
    affiliation: "Amazon Web Services"
repository-code: "https://github.com/spore-host/puffball"
url: "https://spore.host"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - Amazon Braket
  - AWS
  - research computing
  - provenance
  - cost management
